### What are the steps to reproduce this bug?

This bug was found while developing a [Remaining Time](https://github.com/trgkanki/remaining_time) addon.

I'm using `document.cookie` as a persistent storage to store review log and html fragments for FOUC prevention.
It seems like when the cookie list gets sufficiently large, calling API returns erros d/t how `AnkiServer.getSessionBytes` is implemented.

Cookie is the easiest way to inflate HTML request header so this is used as a reproduction step, but I guess anything that can make request header large may cause this, and I think this error may arise on normal circumstances if data races or some kind of lagging occurs.

1. make a new basic note type with front template like:

```html
{{Front}}

<script>
(async function () {
  if (typeof AnkiDroidJS !== 'undefined') {
    document.cookie = 'rt_repro1=' + 'A'.repeat(4000) + '; path=/';
    document.cookie = 'rt_repro2=' + 'A'.repeat(4000) + '; path=/';
    document.cookie = 'rt_repro3=' + 'A'.repeat(4000) + '; path=/';
    document.cookie = 'rt_repro4=' + 'A'.repeat(4000) + '; path=/';
    document.cookie = 'rt_repro5=' + 'A'.repeat(4000) + '; path=/';
    const js = new AnkiDroidJS({ developer: 'repro@example.com', version: '0.0.3' });
    const results = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
      try {
        results.push(await js.ankiGetNewCardCount());
      } catch (e) {
        results.push('ERROR: ' + e);
      }
    }
    alert(JSON.stringify(results));
	document.cookie = 'rt_repro1=; path=/; max-age=0';
	document.cookie = 'rt_repro2=; path=/; max-age=0';
	document.cookie = 'rt_repro3=; path=/; max-age=0';
	document.cookie = 'rt_repro4=; path=/; max-age=0';
	document.cookie = 'rt_repro5=; path=/; max-age=0';
 }
})()
</script>
```

Added a simple apkg file containing such note.
